، تواصل معنا\r\n\r\nأيقونات وسائل التواصل\r\n\r\nبانر رئيسي متحرك (Hero Banner)\r\n\r\nصور احترافية للفنادق في مكة والمدينة\r\n\r\nعبارات تسويقية جذابة\r\n\r\nزر \"احجز الآن\" (يؤدي لواتساب مباشرة)\r\n\r\nمحرك بحث للحجوزات\r\n\r\nالوجهة (مكة / المدينة)\r\n\r\nتاريخ الوصول والمغادرة\r\n\r\nعدد الغرف\r\n\r\nزر \"ابحث\"\r\n\r\nأحدث العروض\r\n\r\nعروض موسمية / باقات خاصة / خصومات\r\n\r\nالفنادق المتوفرة\r\n\r\nعرض سريع لأبرز الفنادق المتاحة في مكة والمدينة\r\n\r\nخدماتنا باختصار\r\n\r\nمختصر لأبرز ما نقدمه مع زر \"اعرف المزيد\"\r\n\r\nآراء العملاء\r\n\r\nتقييمات وتجارب عملاء سابقة\r\n\r\nالأسئلة الشائعة\r\n\r\nأهم الأسئلة وإجاباتها حول الحجز والإقامة\r\n\r\nتذييل الصفحة (Footer)\r\n\r\nالعنوان – رقم الهاتف – روابط التواصل – حقوق النشر\r\n\r\n?‍? صفحة \"من نحن\"\r\nتعريف بالمؤسسة\r\n\r\nرسالتنا\r\n\r\nرؤيتنا\r\n\r\nخبرتنا في مجال الحجوزات\r\n\r\nالتزامنا بخدمة ضيوف الرحمن\r\n\r\n? صفحة \"تواصل معنا\"\r\nنموذج تواصل مباشر (الاسم – رقم الجوال – البريد – الرسالة)\r\n\r\nأزرار التواصل عبر واتساب\r\n\r\nالعنوان وأرقام الهواتف\r\n\r\nخريطة Google Map للمكتب\r\n\r\n?️ صفحة \"خدماتنا\"\r\n1. حجز الغرف في مكة المكرمة\r\nفنادق قريبة من الحرم\r\n\r\nأسعار محدثة – صور – زر حجز عبر واتساب\r\n\r\n2. حجز الغرف في المدينة المنورة\r\nفنادق قرب المسجد النبوي\r\n\r\nتفاصيل كاملة مع إمكانية التواصل المباشر\r\n\r\n3. خدمة التوصيل والنقل\r\nاستقبال من المطار\r\n\r\nتنقل بين مكة والمدينة\r\n\r\nرحلات جماعية وخاصة\r\n\r\n4. باقات العمرة الشاملة (في حال توفر الخدمة)\r\nإقامة + تنقل + تصاريح + إشراف مرشدين\r\n\r\n5. عروض موسمية\r\nخصومات العائلات / الحجز المبكر\r\n\r\nعروض رمضان – الحج – العمرة\r\n٦- حجز طيران تذاكر طيران \r\n\r\n? زر موحّد للحجز:\r\n\r\n\"احجز الآن عبر واتساب\" مع رسالة تلقائية مثل:\r\n\"السلام عليكم، أرغب بحجز غرفة في [المدينة] بتاريخ [..]\"\r\n\r\n✅ ملاحظات تقنية\r\nالموقع يكون متجاوب (Responsive) لكل الأجهزة\r\n\r\nيدعم اللغة العربية كلغة أساسية\r\n\r\nسرعة تحميل عالية\r\n\r\nسهل التحديث وإضافة الفنادق أو العروض\r\n\r\nيفضل الربط المباشر عبر واتساب','2025-04-29 16:38:40','2025-09-14 06:00:39',NULL,0,0,1,NULL,'https://github.dev/Kermina-Milad/ghosn-alzaiton/tree/main','https://github.dev/Ibrahimsamy308/elzaytoon/tree/main'),(288,'Lapmob Market',1,0,0,0,0,1,1,'2025-09-30 00:00:00','2025-05-05',0,NULL,'https://yousab-tech.com/orangestore/PHP/Home.php\r\n\r\nE:\\xampp\\htdocs\\orangestore\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/boula1997/orangestore.git\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nV','2025-05-05 17:12:02','2025-08-29 22:05:36',NULL,0,0,1,NULL,'https://github.com/boula1997/laptopsmarket/tree/main','https://github.dev/boula1997/orangestore/tree/main'),(289,'Beshoy Wassem',0,0,0,1,0,1,1,NULL,'2025-05-10',0,NULL,NULL,'2025-05-10 16:04:06','2025-07-11 03:08:02',NULL,0,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(291,'Courses Website',20000,0,0,0,1,1,1,'2025-09-30 23:00:00','2025-05-14',0,NULL,'https://themeholy.com/html/edura/demo/index.html\n\nhttps://math-4-all-front.vercel.app/','2025-05-15 20:22:42','2025-09-14 04:06:40',NULL,0,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(292,'Courses App',20000,10000,0,1,1,1,1,'2025-09-19 22:56:00','2025-05-14',0,NULL,'https://codecanyon.net/item/valux-lms-react-native-learning-management-template-for-android-and-ios-app/38321923\r\n\r\n\r\nnpx @react-native-community/cli init MyAwesomeApp\r\n\r\nnpx react-native@0.73.3 start --legacy-peer-deps\r\nnpx react-native start \r\nCd android \r\n./gradlew clean\r\ncd ..\r\nnpx react-native run-android\r\n\r\nset JAVA_HOME=\"C:\\Program Files\\Eclipse Adoptium\\jdk-11.0.27.6-hotspot\"\r\nset PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\\bin;%PATH%\r\n\r\n\r\nset JAVA_HOME=C:\\Program Files\\Eclipse Adoptium\\jdk-17.0.15.6-hotspot\r\nset PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\\bin;%PATH%\r\n\r\ncode android\\local.properties\r\nsdk.dir=C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Android\\\\Sdk\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## This file must *NOT* be checked into Version Control Systems,\r\n# as it contains information specific to your local configuration.\r\n#\r\n# Location of the SDK. This is only used by Gradle.\r\n# For customization when using a Version Control System, please read the\r\n# header note.\r\n#Wed May 25 10:56:02 IST 2022\r\nsdk.dir=C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Android\\\\Sdk\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nExpo App\r\nhttps://codecanyon.net/item/educate-online-course-elearning-react-native-expo-ui-kit/51869176\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIntroduction\r\nReact Native Learning Management System App Multipurpose templates. This has been built with React Native CLI! That means UI is compatible for both Android and iOS.\r\n\r\nThis page will help you install and build your first React Native app.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\nDesign with React Native\r\nFor Android & iOS\r\nAndroid 11 Ready\r\nSeparate File for Each Page & Component\r\nSplashScreen\r\nLogin & Signup Page\r\nHome page with Slider\r\nScreen swiper>/li>\r\nProfile & Edit Profile\r\nBeautiful Login, Register & OTP Screen\r\nSearch Page\r\nNotification Page\r\nFavourite Page\r\nAccount Setting Page\r\nApp Setting Page\r\nCarousel Slider\r\nEasy to Understand Code\r\nClean Code\r\nReady to Integrate\r\nCourse Listing Page\r\nExam Module\r\nPrevious Next Question\r\nExam Timer\r\nExam Result Page\r\nChange Settings\r\n... Much More\r\nWhat you will get?\r\nlearning Management App Template\r\nFull source code\r\nDocumentation\r\nFree Version Upgrade\r\nSetup Development Environment\r\nIt requires Xcode or Android Studio to get started. If you already have one of these tools installed, you should be able to get up and running within a few minutes. If they are not installed, you should expect to spend about an hour installing and configuring them.\r\n\r\nThe instructions are a bit different depending on your development operating system, and whether you want to start developing for iOS or Android. If you want to develop for both Android and iOS, that\'s fine - you can pick one to start with, since the setup is a bit different.\r\n\r\nDevelopment OS\r\nmacos\r\nWindow\r\nLinux\r\nTarget os\r\nAndroid\r\niOS\r\nmacos android\r\nInstalling dependencies\r\nYou will need Node, Watchman, the React Native command line interface, a JDK, and Android Studio.\r\n\r\nWhile you can use any editor of your choice to develop your app, you will need to install Android Studio in order to set up the necessary tooling to build your React Native app for Android.\r\n\r\nNode & Watchman\r\nWe recommend installing Node and Watchman using Homebrew. Run the following commands in a Terminal after installing Homebrew:\r\n\r\nhtml												brew install node\r\n													brew install watchman\r\n											\r\nIf you have already installed Node on your system, make sure it is Node 12 or newer.\r\n\r\nOR\r\n\r\nYou\'ll need to install Node.js >=v14.17+ (Recommended Version) (NPM comes along with it) and serve (an NPM package)\r\n\r\nJava Development Kit\r\nWe recommend installing JDK using Homebrew. Run the following commands in a Terminal after installing Homebrew:\r\n\r\nhtml												brew install --cask adoptopenjdk/openjdk/adoptopenjdk11\r\n											\r\nIf you have already installed JDK on your system, make sure it is JDK 11 or newer.\r\n\r\nAndroid development environment\r\n1. Install Android Studio\r\nDownload and install Android Studio. While on Android Studio installation wizard, make sure the boxes next to all of the following items are checked:\r\n\r\nAndroid SDK\r\nAndroid SDK Platform\r\nAndroid Virtual Device\r\nThen, click \"Next\" to install all of these components. Once setup has finalized and you\'re presented with the Welcome screen, proceed to the next step.\r\n\r\n2. Install the Android SDK\r\nAndroid Studio installs the latest Android SDK by default. Building a React Native app with native code, however, requires the Android 11 (R) SDK in particular. Additional Android SDKs can be installed through the SDK Manager in Android Studio. To do that, open Android Studio, click on \"Configure\" button and select \"SDK Manager\".\r\n\r\nThe SDK Manager can also be found within the Android Studio \"Preferences\" dialog, under Appearance & Behavior → System Settings → Android SDK.\r\n\r\nRunning our React Native application\r\nGo to project directory\r\n\r\nhtml													cd valuxLMS\r\n														npx react-native start\r\n												\r\nOpen new terminal go to valuxLMS directory\r\n\r\nhtml													cd valuxLMS\r\n														cd android\r\n														gradlew clean\r\n														cd ..\r\n														npx react-native run-android --variant=release\r\n												\r\nSee the official React Native doc here\r\n\r\nPages and Components Info\r\nSign In (src/Screens/SignInScreen.js)\r\nSign Up (src/Screens/SignUpScreen.js)\r\nOTP Verify (src/Screens/OtpverfyScreen.js)\r\nHome Page (src/Screens/HomeScsreen.js)\r\nExam (src/Screens/ExamScreenfile/ExamScreen.js)\r\nCourse Detail Page (src/Screens/PopularCoursesScreen.js)\r\nInstructor Detail page (src/Screens/InstructorScreen.js)\r\nMy Profile (src/Screens/AccountSetingsScreen.js)\r\nMy Notification (src/Screens/NotificationScreenfile/NotificationScreen.js)\r\nEtc....\r\nCommon Components:\r\nHeader (src/Components/Commonfile/HeaderBackarrow.js)\r\nHome Page Slider (src/Components/SliderScreenAllfile/)\r\nBottom Tab (src/Components/BottomTabAllScreen/)\r\nEtc....\r\nTemplate Features:\r\nReact JS 17.0.1+\r\nBootstrap v5.x\r\nSimple client-side routing (page based)\r\nEasy Customization\r\nReact Native Video/li>\r\nDependencies\r\nHere are the dependencies list which being used in the LMS React Template:\r\n\r\nhtml					\"dependencies\": {\r\n						\"@react-native-async-storage/async-storage\": \"^1.15.17\",\r\n						\"@react-native-community/clipboard\": \"^1.5.1\",\r\n						\"@react-navigation/bottom-tabs\": \"^6.2.0\",\r\n						\"@react-navigation/native\": \"^6.0.8\",\r\n						\"@react-navigation/stack\": \"^6.1.1\",\r\n						\"@twotalltotems/react-native-otp-input\": \"^1.3.11\",\r\n						\"add\": \"^2.0.6\",\r\n						\"or\": \"^0.2.0\",\r\n						\"react\": \"^17.0.2\",\r\n						\"react-icons\": \"^4.3.1\",\r\n						\"react-native\": \"0.67.2\",\r\n						\"react-native-animatable\": \"^1.3.3\",\r\n						\"react-native-animated-loader\": \"^0.0.9\",\r\n						\"react-native-animated-nav-tab-bar\": \"^3.1.7\",\r\n						\"react-native-app-intro-slider\": \"^4.0.4\",\r\n						\"react-native-elements\": \"^3.4.2\",\r\n						\"react-native-gesture-handler\": \"^2.3.2\",\r\n						\"react-native-material-textfield\": \"^0.16.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-pager-view\": \"^5.4.11\",\r\n						\"react-native-paper\": \"^4.11.2\",\r\n						\"react-native-parallax-header\": \"^1.1.4\",\r\n						\"react-native-reanimated\": \"^2.2.4\",\r\n						\"react-native-responsive-screen\": \"^1.4.2\",\r\n						\"react-native-safe-area-context\": \"^3.4.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-screens\": \"^3.13.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-simple-radio-button\": \"^2.7.4\",\r\n						\"react-native-slider\": \"^0.11.0\",\r\n						\"react-native-slider-intro\": \"^1.0.9\",\r\n						\"react-native-snap-carousel\": \"^3.9.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-switch-toggle\": \"^2.2.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-tab-view\": \"^3.1.1\",\r\n						\"react-native-vector-icons\": \"^9.1.0\",\r\n						\"react-native-video\": \"^5.2.0\",\r\n						\"react-navigation\": \"^4.4.4\",\r\n						\"react-swiper\": \"^0.1.5\",\r\n						\"rn-rncviewpager\": \"^1.3.2\",\r\n						\"rn-viewpager\": \"^1.2.9\",\r\n						\"styled-components\": \"^5.3.3\",\r\n						\"yarn\": \"^1.22.18\"\r\n					}\r\n				\r\nFonts Used\r\nBy default, the template loads DM Sans font from Google Web Font Services, you can change the font with the one that suits you best. Google Fonts\r\n\r\ncss					@import url(\'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans&display=swap\');\r\n					$font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif;\r\n				\r\nNote: After SCSS file run then it will be work\r\n\r\nCredits\r\nImages\r\nFreepick\r\nGoogle Font\r\nPackages\r\nReact Native\r\nreact-native-video\r\nreact-native-responsive-screen\r\nGoogle Fonts\r\n24-Hour Turnaround Support:\r\nQuick, Dedicated & Professional Support!\r\n\r\nWe only provide support through our email. Please submit your ticket by sending us email at developer@vginfotec.com.\r\n\r\nFor any pre-purchase query, please use live chat on vginfotec.com, email, and the item’s comment section on ThemeForest. Thanks!','2025-05-15 20:23:33','2025-09-11 03:56:36',NULL,0,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(294,'Celoptra Tourism',8800,4000,0,0,1,1,1,'2025-09-19 23:00:00',NULL,0,'Fgg','https://www.promotravel.tours/en\r\n\r\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/1AawKbhEFG/\r\n\r\nhttps://cleopatra-front.vercel.app/\r\n\r\nhttps://yousab-tech.com/promo/public/en/dashboard\r\n\r\nhttps://cleopatraluxurytravel.com/en\r\nhttps://trinityluxurytravel.com/en\r\nhttps://dashboard.trinityluxurytravel.com/en/dashboard\r\n\r\nhttps://dashboard.cleopatraluxurytravel.com/public/dashboard\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://mandalatours.net/?fbclid=IwdGRjcAMtegtjbGNrAy16kWV4dG4DYWVtAjExAAEePboLJP72m98LBTVce3L0twkY_mpu5fS0q0ZsBKYQ4yci8aD5azbXcjm3ZMo_aem_RHQsEN6OYZ4rHCX6w91_tw\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ntrips (27) 2025-09-15 22:07:39\r\ncountries varchar\r\ncreated_at timestamp\r\ndestination_id bigint\r\nid bigint\r\nnoCities int\r\nnoCountries int\r\nnoDays int\r\nprice double\r\nupdated_at timestamp\r\n\r\ntrip_translations (81) 2025-09-15 22:07:39\r\naccommodation text\r\nactivities text\r\nairport text\r\ncreated_at timestamp\r\ndescription text\r\nguide text\r\nlocale varchar\r\nmeals text\r\ntitle varchar\r\ntransfers text\r\ntrip_id bigint\r\nupdated_at timestamp   \r\n\r\n\r\nwant insert into for this trip conetent and for 3 languages en es pt (portgues)\r\n\r\n\r\nTipping    destination id is 6 and  id should be 45\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEgypt\r\nCountries\r\n\r\n1\r\n\r\nCities\r\n\r\n10\r\n\r\nDays\r\n\r\n11\r\n\r\nPrice\r\n\r\nGet a quote\r\n\r\nOVERVIEW\r\nBrief Summary\r\nDiscover Egypt\r\nEmbark on an unforgettable adventure through Egypt, where you will discover its hidden treasures and historical wonders. You\'ll start in Cairo, exploring the iconic pyramids and Sphinx, before heading into the heart of the country, visiting desert oases and ancient necropolises. Sail down the Nile River on a luxury cruise, visiting majestic temples and ancient cities along the way. With stunning landscapes, rich history and fascinating culture, this trip will immerse you in the magic of Egypt and leave you with memories that will last a lifetime.\r\n\r\nTRIP HIGHLIGHTS\r\nMemorable Experiences\r\nThe Egyptian Museum\r\nThe Egyptian Museum\r\nKarnak\r\nKarnak\r\nAlabaster Mosque\r\nAlabaster Mosque\r\nTemple of Queen Hatshepsut\r\nTemple of Queen Hatshepsut\r\nThe Hanging Church in the Coptic Quarter\r\nThe Hanging Church in the Coptic Quarter\r\nPyramids of Giza\r\nPyramids of Giza\r\nThe Citadel of Saladin\r\nThe Citadel of Saladin\r\nSphinx\r\nSphinx\r\nHatshepsut temple\r\nHatshepsut temple\r\nPlanned travel schedule\r\nITINERARY\r\n\r\nDay 1 (Saturday) - Cairo\r\n\r\nDay 2 (Sunday) - Cairo\r\nDay 2\r\nAfter breakfast, we dive into a full day of exploration in Cairo. We\'ll be amazed by the famous Pyramids of Giza - Keops, Kefren, and Micerinos - and the imposing Sphinx. Next, we\'ll explore the Egyptian Museum, home to the treasures of Tutankhamun. After lunch, our journey continues to the Saladin Citadel and the Alabaster Mosque, concluding with a stroll through the Coptic quarter.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (Monday) - Cairo to Meidum Pyramid, Al Fayum Oasis, Wadi Rayyan, Wadi al Hittan, and Menia\r\n\r\nDay 4 (Tuesday) - Menia to Zawiyyet Sultan, Beni Hassan, Deir Al Muharraq, Tombs of Mir, and Assiut\r\n\r\nDay 5 (Wednesday) - Assiut to Sohag, Abydos, and Luxor\r\n\r\nDay 6 (Thursday) - Luxor\r\n\r\nDay 7 (Friday) - Luxor to Esna\r\n\r\nDay 8 (Saturday) - Esna to Edfu, Kom Ombo, Aswan\r\n\r\nDay 9 (Sunday) - Aswan\r\n\r\nDay 10 (Monday) - Aswan to Cairo\r\n\r\nDay 11 (Tuesday) - Cairo\r\nWhat\'s Included in the Tour\r\nAirport\r\nMeet & Assist (Arrival & Departure)\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n4 nights on a Cruise (Luxor/Aswan) (Full Board)\r\n3 nights in Cairo (Bed & Breakfast)\r\n1 night in Menia (Half Board)\r\n1 night in Assiut (Half Board)\r\n1 night in Luxor (Bed & Breakfast)\r\nTransfers\r\nTransfers in modern air-conditioned tourist vehicles\r\n\r\nActivities\r\nVisits to the Pyramids of Giza complex, including the Pyramids of Khufu, Khafre, and Menkaure; Egyptian Museum, Citadel, Alabaster Mosque and Coptic Cairo.\r\nMeidum Pyramid in Meidum.\r\nTunis Village in Al Fayoum Oasis.\r\nValley of the Whales and Whale Fossil Museum in Wadi Al Hitan.\r\nBeni Hassan Necropolis, Tombs of Mir.\r\nDeir Al Muharraq Monastery, White and Red Monasteries in Sohag.\r\nTemple of Abydos.\r\nKarnak and Luxor Temples.\r\nThe Luxor Museum\r\nValley of the Kings, Medinet Habu, Deir el-Bahari, Deir el Medina and Colossi of Memnon.\r\nTemples of Edfu and Kom Ombo.\r\nGranite Quarry, Unfinished Obelisk.\r\nHigh Dam, Felucca ride, and Philae Temple in Aswan.\r\nGuide\r\nThere will be an English-speaking guide during the visits.\r\n\r\nRequest a quote\r\nName*\r\nEnter name\r\nCompany name*\r\nEnter company name\r\nEmail*\r\nEnter email\r\nMobile Number\r\nMobile Number\r\nMore Details\r\nEnter more details\r\nSubmit\r\nData submitted successfully\r\nwarning\r\nThe order of the scheduled visits may change due to unforeseen circumstances, but the content of the tour will always be respected\r\n\r\nWhat\'s excluded from the tour\r\nlogo\r\nInternational or domestic flights\r\nlogo\r\nPersonal spending\r\nlogo\r\nEntry visa fees\r\nlogo\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nV','2025-08-23 03:11:05','2025-09-24 07:08:11',NULL,0,1,0,NULL,'https://github.dev/boula1997/cleopatra-front/tree/main','https://github.dev/boula1997/promo/tree/main');
